  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 124 PM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nRain will continue intermittently through Thursday and will \nslowly taper off late Thursday night. Expect winds to remain\nelevated through the rest of the week at at least 20 mph during\nthe daytime hours. Our cold front moves through by Friday\nmorning and we will feel the cold air advection with this front.\nWinds flip out of the north and we'll feel a brisk gusty wind \nnear 35 mph with mostly cloudy skies to start Friday and it'll \nfeel chilly with morning temperatures in the upper 40s to lower\n50s. Clouds clear throughout the day and temperatures only reach\nthe upper 50s to lower 60s across the area making it truly feel\nlike fall.\n\nThese fall-like temperatures stick around through the weekend\nwith a chance for our first frost possible on Saturday morning\nwith lows dipping into the mid 30s in a few places. Highs stick\nin the 60s and 70s with lows in the 40s through the weekend as\nhigh pressure builds back over the area. No rain is expected for\nthe start of next week.",
